IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `cpi-il35-nouns`

-- ===========================================================================
-- PUBLISHED DATA, NOT LAW. Generated; do not edit by hand.
-- Regenerate and diff:  python3 tools/gen_published_figures.py --check
--
-- The general consumer price index (code 120010, 'מדד המחירים לצרכן - כללי') as the
-- Central Bureau of Statistics publishes it through its public index API: every month from
-- January 2000 to August 2026, 320 readings, each in the base in force when it was published.
-- The Laws that use the index (Income Tax Ordinance s 1 'מדד', s 120B; National Insurance Law
-- s 1 'מדד', s 334(a)(1)) say only 'the consumer price index the Bureau publishes'; the numbers are the
-- Bureau's, not the Knesset's, and they are not law.
--
-- [cbs-cpi] cbs-cpi-general-120010-2000-01-to-2026-08.json
--   url:        https://api.cbs.gov.il/index/data/price?id=120010&format=json&download=false&startPeriod=01-2000&endPeriod=09-2026&PageSize=400
--   retrieved:  2026-10-08T22:26:58Z (CBS public index API (api.cbs.gov.il), GET through the il-central-1 proxy)
--   sha256:     11a1b271fd303b3109a761556ae2effb4aaa2e3762f9ac05886c10404e09eeb8   (49836 bytes)
-- [cbs-cpi-coef] cbs-cpi-general-120010-2000-01-to-2026-08-with-linkage-coefficients.json
--   url:        https://api.cbs.gov.il/index/data/price?id=120010&format=json&download=false&startPeriod=01-2000&endPeriod=09-2026&PageSize=400&coef=true
--   retrieved:  2026-10-08T22:27:03Z
--   sha256:     cf440d64bf194af029f721149efa4fb1cbf7f1f73c2703e1c36d0589242b00f9   (376107 bytes)
--   Both sit in ../../registers/source-bundle/data/ beside SOURCES.json, which records the above.
--   The two files give the same 320 readings and percentages; the second adds the Bureau's linkage
--   coefficients (prevBase), which this module carries as the step factors below.
--
-- THE BASES. The Bureau re-bases the index from time to time (the index of the base period is 100).
-- A reading is published in the base in force that month and is never restated here. In this series:
--   base 1998 ('1998 ממוצע'): 12 readings, 2000-01 to 2000-12
--   base 2000 ('2000 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2001-01 to 2002-12
--   base 2002 ('2002 ממוצע'): 48 readings, 2003-01 to 2006-12
--   base 2006 ('2006 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2007-01 to 2008-12
--   base 2008 ('2008 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2009-01 to 2010-12
--   base 2010 ('2010 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2011-01 to 2012-12
--   base 2012 ('2012 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2013-01 to 2014-12
--   base 2014 ('2014 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2015-01 to 2016-12
--   base 2016 ('2016 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2017-01 to 2018-12
--   base 2018 ('2018 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2019-01 to 2020-12
--   base 2020 ('2020 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2021-01 to 2022-12
--   base 2022 ('2022 ממוצע'): 24 readings, 2023-01 to 2024-12
--   base 2024 ('2024 ממוצע'): 20 readings, 2025-01 to 2026-08
-- Within a base, readings compare directly. Across a change of base they do not, until one is
-- restated in the other's base: the Bureau's linkage coefficient links the two bases (a reading in the newer
-- base times the coefficient is the same index in the older base). The coefficients are constant for a
-- pair of bases across all rows of both files, and the cumulative products reproduce every `value` in
-- the linkage file (checked by the generator on every run).
--
-- WHEN A READING IS PUBLISHED. The Laws speak of 'the index published last before' a day. The files carry no
-- publication date. SOURCES.json ('latest_reading') records: 'August 2026 (published in September 2026); the September 2026 reading is not yet published at retrieval'. So a month's reading is published in the
-- following month. That each reading is published after the first and before the last day of the following month
-- (in practice on the 15th) is ASSUMED, NOT READ from any deposited source; it is the only fact about publication the
-- encoding uses (NOTES.md, assumption A1).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Consumer price index readings published by the Central Bureau of Statistics — published data, not law`

@ref [cbs-cpi] sha256 11a1b271...; SOURCES.json 'latest_reading'; assumption A1
`the number of months from the month a reading is of to the month it is published in` MEANS 1

@ref [cbs-cpi] first row, 2000-01
`the first month of the published series` MEANS `A calendar month` WITH `year of the month` IS 2000, `number of the month in the year` IS 1

@ref [cbs-cpi] last row, 2026-08
`the last month of the published series` MEANS `A calendar month` WITH `year of the month` IS 2026, `number of the month in the year` IS 8

-- The base years of the series, oldest first.
@ref [cbs-cpi] currBase.baseDesc of each row
`the base years of the published series, oldest first` MEANS LIST 1998, 2000, 2002, 2006, 2008, 2010, 2012, 2014, 2016, 2018, 2020, 2022, 2024

-- The Bureau's linkage coefficient from the next newer base into the base named: a reading in that next newer
-- base, times this factor, is the same index in the base named. (A newer base's step to its predecessor.)
@ref [cbs-cpi-coef] prevBase.coeff; constant across rows (generator-checked)
GIVEN `the base year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`the step factor into base` `the base year` MEANS
    BRANCH IF `the base year` EQUALS 1998 THEN JUST 1.064  -- 1998 ממוצע from 2000 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2000 THEN JUST 1.068  -- 2000 ממוצע from 2002 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2002 THEN JUST 1.038  -- 2002 ממוצע from 2006 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2006 THEN JUST 1.051  -- 2006 ממוצע from 2008 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2008 THEN JUST 1.061  -- 2008 ממוצע from 2010 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2010 THEN JUST 1.052  -- 2010 ממוצע from 2012 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2012 THEN JUST 1.02  -- 2012 ממוצע from 2014 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2014 THEN JUST 0.989  -- 2014 ממוצע from 2016 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2016 THEN JUST 1.01  -- 2016 ממוצע from 2018 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2018 THEN JUST 1.003  -- 2018 ממוצע from 2020 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2020 THEN JUST 1.059  -- 2020 ממוצע from 2022 ממוצע
           IF `the base year` EQUALS 2022 THEN JUST 1.074  -- 2022 ממוצע from 2024 ממוצע
           OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- THE READINGS, oldest first. Fields: year, month, base year, value, percent published for the month,
